   $q$A community garden is shaped like a trapezoid with parallel sides of $20$ m and $12$ m that are $8$ m apart. A square shed that is $3$ m on each side sits inside the garden. How many square meters of the garden are left for planting?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$119$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$247$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-halve-trapezoid-area"},{"text":"$116$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-shed-perimeter"},{"text":"$128$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-the-shed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$119$$q$, $q$The trapezoid has area $\frac{1}{2} \times (20 + 12) \times 8 = 128$ square meters, and the shed covers $3 \times 3 = 9$, so $128 - 9 = 119$ square meters are left. The choice $116$ subtracts $12$, which is the shed's perimeter, not its area.$q$, 'draft', null)
